WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.462
Lesson one.

00:00:01.462 --> 00:00:08.957
Before we evolve anything, let's look at the problem: what the lander senses, what it can do, and how it is scored.

00:00:09.557 --> 00:00:13.086
This is Lunar Lander, from the Gymnasium library.

00:00:13.086 --> 00:00:17.359
The lander starts high above the surface, with a random push.

00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:21.560
The goal is to touch down softly between the two flags.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.369
At every step, the lander senses eight numbers.

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:27.936
Its position, measured from the pad.

00:00:27.936 --> 00:00:30.386
Its horizontal and vertical speed.

00:00:30.386 --> 00:00:33.070
Its tilt, and how fast it is spinning.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:37.454
And two switches that say whether each leg touches the ground.

00:00:38.054 --> 00:00:41.740
And at every step, it must choose one of four actions.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:47.031
Do nothing, fire the left engine, fire the main engine, or fire the right engine.

00:00:47.031 --> 00:00:52.147
So whatever our network looks like, it has eight inputs and four outputs.

00:00:52.747 --> 00:00:55.834
The game itself hands out points as it goes.

00:00:55.834 --> 00:01:00.465
Moving toward the pad, slowing down and staying level all earn points.

00:01:00.465 --> 00:01:04.149
Drifting away, speeding up and tilting cost them.

00:01:04.749 --> 00:01:06.970
There are also one-off events.

00:01:06.970 --> 00:01:10.359
Each leg that touches the ground earns ten points.

00:01:10.359 --> 00:01:12.638
Coming to rest earns a hundred.

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:16.386
A crash, or flying off the screen, costs a hundred.

00:01:16.986 --> 00:01:18.742
And fuel isn't free.

00:01:18.742 --> 00:01:25.015
Every frame the main engine fires costs a little, and the side engines cost a tenth of that.

00:01:25.015 --> 00:01:28.388
So hovering forever is a losing strategy.

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:33.274
Add it all up over one flight, and you get the episode's reward.

00:01:33.274 --> 00:01:36.787
An average of two hundred or more counts as solved.

00:01:36.787 --> 00:01:40.599
That reward is exactly what we will use as fitness.
